  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "The sum of all but one of the interior angles of a convex polygon equals \\(2570^\\circ.\\) The remaining angle is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(90^\\circ\\)",
    "B": "\\(105^\\circ\\)",
    "C": "\\(120^\\circ\\)",
    "D": "\\(130^\\circ\\)",
    "E": "\\(144^\\circ\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Let \\(\\theta\\) be the remaining interior angle. Convexity gives \\(0^\\circ<\\theta<180^\\circ\\), so the full interior angle sum satisfies\n\\[2570^\\circ<2570^\\circ+\\theta<2750^\\circ.\\]\nFor an \\(n\\)-sided polygon, where \\(n\\ge3\\) is an integer, the full sum is \\((n-2)180^\\circ\\). It must therefore be a multiple of \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\nThe neighboring multiples are \\(2520^\\circ\\), \\(2700^\\circ\\), and \\(2880^\\circ\\), so only \\(2700^\\circ\\) lies in the required interval. Consequently,\n\\[\\theta=2700^\\circ-2570^\\circ=130^\\circ.\\]\nThe answer is choice D.",
